The usual reason is that binaries cause a significant network load for
no obvious benefit. The way usenet operates the messages are not stored
centrally but rather copied betwen servers, which is no problem for the
usual text messages but a bunch of binaries can easily overload the
system. 
Aditionally many people download all the messages in the groups they
subscribed to in a block to read them offline. Again this is no problem
for text messages but a few unwanted binaries will make you swear and
curse when you've only got ISDN (or even an analog modem).

